# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# portfolio-FE — environment template
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. NEVER commit a filled-in file.
#
# On Cloudflare (Workers Builds) set these under "Settings -> Variables and
# Secrets". `API_URL` must be a BUILD variable (see the note below).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- API origin (SERVER-SIDE ONLY) -----------------------------------------
# Absolute origin of the NestJS API on Render, e.g.
#   https://portfolio-be.onrender.com
#
# This is used for two things:
#   1. The `/api/*` rewrite in next.config.ts, which proxies the browser's
#      same-origin requests to the API. That proxy is what keeps the admin
#      auth cookie working (see DEPLOYMENT.md).
#   2. Server-side rendering fetches (lib/api.ts).
#
# The rewrite destination is resolved at BUILD time, so this must be present
# as a build variable on Cloudflare. Without it the app boots but /api/*
# requests are not proxied and the admin panel cannot authenticate.
API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# --- Browser-visible API base (OPTIONAL) -----------------------------------
# Leave this UNSET in production.
#
# Setting it to the Render URL makes the browser call the API cross-site
# (workers.dev -> onrender.com). The auth cookie is SameSite=Lax, so the
# browser would drop it and the admin panel would silently fail to log in.
# The relative "/api" default is proxied same-origin and is the correct
# production setup. Set it only for local testing against a remote API.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# --- Public site metadata (OPTIONAL) ---------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://portfolio.example.workers.dev
